// v0.1.434: `exit 0` is a program saying it succeeded, and on the Wasm
// backend it used to come back as 1 -- the emission dropped the code and
// trapped, and every host reads a trap as a failure.
//
// This file is here for two reasons at once. It is the only parity program
// that calls `exit`, so it is what reaches the gated `wasm_exit_used` runtime
// section (test/parity/SECTIONS); and the parity harness compares exit status
// against the interpreter's, so it is also where a backend that turns a
// successful exit into a failure is caught by the ordinary suite rather than
// only by scripts/exit_status_check.sh.
//
// A nonzero status cannot live here: the harness SKIPs any program the
// interpreter does not exit 0 on, and its failure section is built for
// programs that fail with a diagnostic. exit_status_check covers that half.
let _ = print "done" in
exit 0
